`,i.jsx(c.p,{children:'When a model is trained repeatedly on data generated by other models, the distribution of its outputs tends to narrow. Rare modes disappear first, then the tails shrink, and eventually the model produces a handful of "safe" answers for almost every prompt. 이 현상은 흔히 model collapse 라고 부르며, 합성 데이터의 비율이 높아질수록 더 빨리 나타납니다. The question is not whether diversity decreases, but which parts of it we can afford to lose and which parts we must protect.'}),`
